WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.710
It's Wednesday, November 4, and this is the Transhuman Daily.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.030
Here's your day in transhumanism, in 3 minutes flat.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.200
Self-improvement.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:21.570
Anthropic says AI helping build AI may soon dramatically speed up progress.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:23.540
And in an early trial,

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:27.660
doctors fixed a faulty DNA letter inside a patient's liver.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:35.590
In AI, a new tool designs proteins from a plain description,

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:38.260
like 'glow green' or 'break down plastic'.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:40.060
Meanwhile,

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:46.350
China's BrainCo plans a brain-stimulating wearable to curb appetite: an 'electronic GLP-1'.

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:51.170
A brain-inspired chip read emotions from brainwave recordings in microseconds,

00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:53.300
on about a fortieth of the energy.

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:59.120
And AI agents now help run a telescope listening for alien signals. Nothing yet.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.460
In the longevity lab, a fatty acid made worn-out cells self-destruct,

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:06.530
and cleared some from old mice.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:11.070
And ring-shaped RNA rewound aged stem cells in a dish,

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:13.050
without the risky full reset.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.080
In an early trial,

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:21.290
Muna says its pill nudged older volunteers' brain-fluid markers toward younger levels.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:26.540
And ten blood proteins spotted ALS with 98% accuracy,

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:29.210
well ahead of today's best marker.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:35.960
For wellbeing, 44% of drinkers on GLP-1 drugs say they now drink less.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:40.510
And an early trial is aiming gentle ultrasound de

00:01:40.510 --> 00:01:43.510
ep in the brain to quiet voices in schizophrenia.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.690
Now, the catch. As Australia readies three-parent IVF,

00:01:48.690 --> 00:01:52.440
studies show the mother's mitochondria can creep back.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:56.170
And blueberries for depression? That pilot had just 18 people,

00:01:56.170 --> 00:01:58.480
and the difference wasn't significant.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:02.530
Meanwhile,

00:02:02.530 --> 00:02:07.840
six humanoid robots worked a 24-hour shift in a Chinese convenience store, live.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:10.840
Jumping spiders seem to have REM-like sleep,

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:13.310
and they catch up on it after a rough night.

00:02:15.470 --> 00:02:20.320
Plus, a hand-cranked gadget reads your blood type from one drop in a minute.

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:21.410
No power needed.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:25.980
Smarter AI, self-repairing cells, healthier habits.

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:28.500
Self-improvement just got new tools.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.510
Zoom out, and the line only goes up.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.440
And the future keeps arriving ahead of schedule.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.970
One day, all of this. Tomorrow, probably more.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.170
You've been watching the Transhuman Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.160
Live long. See you tomorrow.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.600
Want more? Meet us in North Sydney on November 27.
